{
  "uid": "meizuno-overview",
  "title": "Meizuno — Overview",
  "description": "Stack health, host, and error logs up front; Traefik, the databases and monitoring's own footprint in collapsed rows. Provisioned from git — edit grafana/dashboards/meizuno-overview.json, because the file overrides UI changes on reload.",
  "tags": [
    "meizuno",
    "provisioned"
  ],
  "editable": true,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timezone": "browser",
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Units and how to read this",
      "collapsed": true,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "Units and conventions",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 22,
            "w": 24,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 1
          },
          "options": {
            "mode": "markdown",
            "content": "## Units on this dashboard\n\n| On screen | Unit | What it measures |\n|---|---|---|\n| `%` | percent | Share of a capacity: CPU across all 6 cores, RAM of total, connections of `max_connections`, 5xx of all requests. |\n| `B` `KiB` `MiB` `GiB` | bytes, **binary** | 1 KiB = 1024 B, 1 MiB = 1024 KiB. Grafana shows IEC units, so `111.9 MiB` is ~117 MB in decimal marketing units. |\n| `B/s` | bytes per second | Throughput — disk and network. |\n| `req/s` | requests per second | Traefik, averaged over 5 minutes. |\n| `s` `ms` | seconds | Request latency. |\n| `CPU s/s` | CPU-seconds per second | `1.0` means one core fully busy for the whole interval. |\n| plain number | count | Targets down, log lines, connections, Redis keys, active series. |\n\n## How to read it\n\n**Percentiles.** `p95 = 0.4 s` means 95% of requests finished faster than 0.4 s and 5% took longer. `p50` is the median. Watch p95 and p99 rather than an average — an average hides the slow tail, which is exactly the part users notice.\n\n**Rates are 5-minute averages** (`rate(...[5m])`). A short spike therefore looks smaller than it was and takes a few minutes to appear at full height. For anything sharper, narrow the time range.\n\n**Log levels** come from Loki's `detected_level`, assigned heuristically at ingest. It is dependable for plain-text logs (Go slog, uvicorn) but misses some lines from **forma** and **english**, which emit structured JSON — for those, query `| json | level =~ \"warn|error\"` instead of relying on the level filter.\n\n**Empty panels are not always broken.** `5xx share` divides by total requests, so it is blank at zero traffic; latency percentiles need a few requests to exist; `Redis hit rate` stays blank until something reads from Redis.\n\n**`Disk free — /`** reads the root filesystem explicitly. If it shows *No data*, node-exporter is not labelling the root mount as `/` — check *Free space per filesystem* below for the actual mountpoint names.\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Stack health",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Targets down (count)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "victoriametrics"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 2
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "count(up == 0) or vector(0)",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "none",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "description": "Scrape targets not answering. Should be 0 — anything else means an exporter or a service is down."
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Errors — last 1h (count)",
      "datasource": {
