    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Disk free — / (GiB)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "victoriametrics"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 7
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "node_filesystem_avail_bytes{job=\"node\",mountpoint=\"/\"}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "decimals": 1,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 10000000000
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 20000000000
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "description": "Free space on the ROOT filesystem. An earlier version took min() across all filesystems and ended up reporting /boot/efi (a ~100 MiB vfat partition) instead — alarming and useless. If this reads No data, node-exporter is not labelling the root mount as \"/\"; check the trend panel below for the real mountpoint names. This is the stack's nearest risk: Loki has no disk-space limiter of its own."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Free space per filesystem (GiB)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "victoriametrics"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "node_filesystem_avail_bytes{job=\"node\",fstype=~\"ext2|ext3|ext4|xfs|btrfs|vfat\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{mountpoint}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "pointSize": 8
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "min"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "description": "With alerting deferred, the slope of these lines is the only early warning there is. Small partitions such as /boot/efi show up here too — that is fine in a trend, it was only misleading as a headline number."
    },
